Subject: Check strncmp before indexing (*ep)[nl] in recursively_expand_for_file
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: In recursively_expand_for_file(), (*ep)[nl] == '=' was evaluated before strncmp(*ep, v->name, nl) == 0, causing an out-of-bounds read whenever an environment entry is shorter than nl bytes. Swapping the operands ensures strncmp stops at the NUL terminator before (*ep)[nl] is accessed (portable C without <stdfil.h>).
Upstream-Status: Pending
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: 8553fcd026b9

--- a/src/expand.c
+++ b/src/expand.c
@@ -116,7 +116,7 @@
       /* We could create a hash for the original environment for speed, but a
          reasonably written makefile shouldn't hit this situation...  */
       for (ep = environ; *ep != 0; ++ep)
-        if ((*ep)[nl] == '=' && strncmp (*ep, v->name, nl) == 0)
+        if (strncmp (*ep, v->name, nl) == 0 && (*ep)[nl] == '=')
           return xstrdup ((*ep) + nl + 1);
 
       /* If there's nothing in the parent environment, use the empty string.
